{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-f21e3be1-4735-43ff-a100-7ecc6d6bef99","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-82aea3d11ac8101d","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-9020-oiz46n95/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9020-E001.md","content":"# AMD Instinct ROCm validation campaign for vLLM serving\n\n## Description\n\nRun a functional and performance parity validation campaign for vLLM serving\nof the platform's supported model set on physical AMD Instinct accelerators,\nproducing the per-model go/no-go data that determines the scope of ROCm\nserving runtime productization. This epic resolves the strategy's central\nunknown — whether upstream vLLM ROCm builds reach functional and performance\nparity with the productized CUDA builds for the models RHOAI supports — which\nno readable artifact can answer; the answer must be produced by executing the\ncampaign on hardware.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Define the validation test matrix covering every model in the supported\n  model set for vLLM serving, including the serving configurations and AMD\n  Instinct hardware topology used for each run.\n- Execute functional validation per model: serving behavior and output\n  correctness compared against the CUDA baseline on the same model set.\n- Execute performance validation per model: throughput and latency parity\n  data versus the CUDA baseline.\n- Record per-model results with hardware, driver, and ROCm image versions\n  used for each run.\n- Produce a final report stating a go/no-go recommendation per model and the\n  resulting productization scope (the set of models that clear).\n- Securing AMD Instinct hardware access (procurement or partner lab) is part\n  of this epic's work; the access path is unresolved (see Risks and Notes).\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- A validation plan and test matrix exists that covers every model in the\n  supported model set, recording the serving configurations and hardware\n  topology used.\n- Functional results are recorded per model as pass/fail against the CUDA\n  baseline for the same model set.\n- Performance parity data (throughput and latency) is recorded per model\n  against the CUDA baseline.\n- A final report states a go/no-go recommendation per model and the resulting\n  productization scope.\n- All recorded results originate from executions on physical AMD Instinct\n  hardware, with the hardware, driver, and ROCm image versions documented.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- HLR-1 (P0): validation campaign on physical AMD Instinct hardware\n  establishing functional and performance parity data for vLLM serving of the\n  supported model set, producing the go/no-go scope for productization.\n\n## Risks and Notes\n\n- **Hardware access (availability precondition, externally controlled):**\n  dedicated AMD Instinct nodes do not exist in the CI fleet, and procurement\n  vs. partner-lab access is unresolved. This gates campaign start and cannot\n  be compressed by engineering effort; it is a risk, not an acceptance\n  criterion — the epic's deliverable (the validated report) is what the ACs\n  measure. Partner-lab terms may additionally constrain which models can be\n  run and whether performance numbers are publication-grade.\n- **Upstream ROCm image cadence:** the campaign consumes upstream ROCm builds\n  of vLLM, whose release timing is controlled by AMD and the upstream\n  communities; available versions may constrain the test matrix.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":46201,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-80975552566df778","agent_id":"ab25707c369bcec5a","session_id":"e88daf40-577f-4130-9c11-b6a9bfbaa4d6","uuid":"9b5ab9fe-c507-4948-9cfd-f3895e0eec03","timestamp":"2026-10-26T18:16:14.019Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-9020"}
