{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-7b1cd4cf-1471-44ff-bcb9-306d993673d4","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-8a27eabb4008ef4e","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-9020-oiz46n95/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9020-E002.md","content":"# Productize supported vLLM ROCm serving runtime\n\n## Description\n\nProductize a supported vLLM ROCm serving runtime for the models cleared by\nthe AMD Instinct validation campaign: build and release the ROCm runtime\nimage variant, package it as a platform serving runtime, and validate KServe\ncompatibility on AMD GPU nodes. The runtime's supported scope is definitionally\nthe set of models the validation campaign clears; if fewer models clear than\nthe full supported set, this epic productizes the cleared subset.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Build and release a vLLM ROCm runtime image variant from the midstream vLLM\n  repo, pinned to a recorded ROCm base image version from upstream releases.\n- Configure the Konflux build pipeline for the ROCm image variant in the\n  already-onboarded Serving Runtimes build machinery (no separate onboarding\n  needed — the component is Konflux-onboarded).\n- Define and ship the ServingRuntime (or ClusterServingRuntime) for the ROCm\n  vLLM runtime, requesting amd.com/gpu resources and targeting AMD Instinct\n  nodes.\n- Validate KServe compatibility (KServe itself requires no code changes —\n  accelerator support is runtime-level): InferenceServices using the ROCm\n  serving runtime deploy and reach Ready on AMD GPU nodes.\n- Record the supported (cleared) model set in the runtime's support\n  metadata.\n- Ensure coexistence with existing CUDA-based serving runtimes — the ROCm\n  runtime is additive; existing runtimes are unaffected.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- A vLLM ROCm runtime image build exists in the midstream repo, pinned to a\n  recorded ROCm base image version.\n- The Konflux build pipeline for the ROCm image variant is green.\n- A ServingRuntime CR deploys the ROCm vLLM runtime with amd.com/gpu\n  resource requests for the cleared model set.\n- KServe InferenceServices using the ROCm serving runtime reach Ready on AMD\n  GPU nodes.\n- Existing CUDA-based serving runtimes deploy and serve unchanged (no\n  regression; the new runtime is additive).\n- The supported (cleared) model set is recorded in the runtime's support\n  metadata.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- HLR-2 (P0): a supported vLLM ROCm serving runtime is productized for the\n  models the validation campaign clears.\n- Supports HLR-4 inputs: the recorded supported model set feeds the\n  documentation.\n\n## Risks and Notes\n\n- **Upstream ROCm image cadence (externally controlled):** whether AMD's\n  runtime image releases align with our release trains is outside our\n  control; a pinning/mirroring strategy for the ROCm base image may be\n  needed to keep the productized runtime aligned with release trains.\n- Scope is gated by the validation campaign's go/no-go outcome: if no models\n  clear, productization is cancelled and the campaign report feeds a\n  follow-up strategy decision.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":47066,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-80975552566df778","agent_id":"ab25707c369bcec5a","session_id":"e88daf40-577f-4130-9c11-b6a9bfbaa4d6","uuid":"677081ea-612b-40cf-8d7c-6e77e0c0b224","timestamp":"2026-10-26T18:16:26.230Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-9020"}
