-GPU PyTorchJob requesting amd.com/gpu resources runs to completion\n55\t  on AMD Instinct nodes with distributed initialization across workers.\n56\t- Verified/pinned PyTorch ROCm worker image references are documented for\n57\t  supported training jobs.\n58\t- Existing NVIDIA GPU PyTorchJob execution is unaffected (no regression; AMD\n59\t  support is additive).\n60\t\n61\t## HLR Traceability\n62\t\n63\t- HLR-3 (P1): PyTorch training on ROCm is supported for single- and\n64\t  multi-GPU jobs admitted through Kueue, with amd.com/gpu quota handling\n65\t  (quota/admission side covered by the Distributed Workloads epic).\n66\t\n67\t## Risks and Notes\n68\t\n69\t- **Physical hardware dependency:** validation requires physical AMD Instinct\n70\t  nodes, the same hardware whose access path (procurement vs. partner lab) is\n71\t  unresolved for the serving validation campaign. This is a shared\n72\t  resource-coordination risk, not a structural dependency on the serving\n73\t  campaign's outcome — training enablement proceeds independently.\n74\t- PyTorch ROCm worker images are published upstream; no upstream\n75\t  contribution is required, but available image versions follow the upstream\n76\t  release cadence.\n77\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a65eaf4ef9234320","agent_id":"a06cde2741e62ef88","session_id":"e88daf40-577f-4130-9c11-b6a9bfbaa4d6","uuid":"508f5ef3-4bf0-4371-96ac-1b22379f6a4a","timestamp":"2026-10-26T18:19:03.351Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-a2869adc8bc8186c","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-9020 decomposition"}
