ngle-GPU PyTorchJob requesting amd.com/gpu is admitted through Kueue\n53\t  against the configured quota.\n54\t- A multi-GPU PyTorchJob requesting amd.com/gpu is admitted with\n55\t  all-or-nothing semantics under the amd.com/gpu quota.\n56\t- Quota accounting for amd.com/gpu is correct: usage of admitted workloads is\n57\t  reflected in quota consumption, and workloads queue when quota is\n58\t  exhausted.\n59\t- Existing NVIDIA GPU quota handling and admission behave unchanged.\n60\t\n61\t## HLR Traceability\n62\t\n63\t- HLR-3 (P1): PyTorch training on ROCm is supported for single- and\n64\t  multi-GPU jobs admitted through Kueue, with amd.com/gpu quota handling\n65\t  (job execution side covered by the Training Operator epic).\n66\t\n67\t## Risks and Notes\n68\t\n69\t- **Physical hardware dependency:** end-to-end admission validation requires\n70\t  AMD GPU nodes and a runnable ROCm training workload; this shares the\n71\t  unresolved AMD hardware access path with the serving validation campaign\n72\t  (resource-coordination risk, not a structural dependency).\n73\t- Coordinating a shared end-to-end validation run (a multi-GPU ROCm\n74\t  PyTorchJob admitted under amd.com/gpu quota) with the Training Operator\n75\t  work is a planning concern; each side's acceptance criteria can be verified\n76\t  independently.\n77\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a65eaf4ef9234320","agent_id":"a06cde2741e62ef88","session_id":"e88daf40-577f-4130-9c11-b6a9bfbaa4d6","uuid":"dc20bc20-7fef-483b-84c8-1cbf6e9a02d8","timestamp":"2026-10-26T18:19:04.121Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-97cb929d46211f44","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-9020 decomposition"}
