96\tthe per-model matrix; source_accessibility 0 because the parity data must be\n97\tproduced by execution, not read; cluster_hardware_dependence -2 for the\n98\tdedicated-node requirement). Implementation signal rationales are justified\n99\tand verifiable: E002's open_questions -1 / external_dependency -1 match the\n100\tcampaign gate and upstream ROCm cadence; E005's human_process_gates -1 matches\n101\tthe mandated technical-review AC. The `architecture_claims: 1` rationales cite\n102\tspecific architecture-context files, and all citations were verified against\n103\t`.context`: serving-runtimes.md (only CUDA productized, ROCm not shipped,\n104\tmidstream opendatahub-io/vllm, Konflux onboarded), training-operator.md\n105\t(Kueue admission, NVIDIA GPU Operator nodes), distributed-workloads.md\n106\t(ClusterQueue/LocalQueue quota model, waitForPodsReady all-or-nothing). No\n107\tcalibration misses; no arithmetic checked (pipeline-computed).\n108\t\n109\t### 6. Acceptance Criteria Quality (2/2)\n110\tEvery epic has testable ACs derived from HLR wording. Rule-mandated ACs are\n111\tpresent: E002 carries the Rule 25 \"Konflux build pipeline green\" AC plus a\n112\tno-regression/coexistence AC for existing CUDA runtimes (additive change, so\n113\tno rollback AC is required — it is not a replacement); E005 carries the\n114\ttechnical-review-against-implementation AC. The strategy's\n115\texternally-controlled preconditions are correctly filed: hardware access is a\n116\tRisks/Notes entry on E001 (with the AC placed on the deliverable — recorded\n117\tresults with documented versions), and upstream cadence is a risk on E002 —\n118\tno soft ACs found. No epic body references sibling epics by draft ID (E003\n119\tand E004 refer to each other by component name, not ID).\n120\t\n121\t### 7. Completeness (2/2)\n122\tFull strategy scope is accounted for: all four HLRs, the out-of-scope\n123\tcommitments (non-AMD accelerators, GPU sharing/partitioning) carried as\n124\texplic