{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-922bd317edbf0add","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9020-E002\n3\ttitle: Productize supported vLLM ROCm serving runtime\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9020\n5\tcomponent: Serving Runtimes\n6\tteam: RHOAI Serving\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tdependencies:\n10\t- RHAISTRAT-9020-E001\n11\tgated_by: RHAISTRAT-9020-E001\n12\tgate_failure_impact:\n13\t  action: rewrite\n14\t  fallback_approach: 'Scope is the set of models the validation campaign clears: if\n15\t    a subset clears, productize that subset; if no models clear, productization is\n16\t    cancelled and the campaign report feeds a follow-up strategy decision.'\n17\tai_signals:\n18\t  change_specificity: 0\n19\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n20\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n21\t  existing_foundation: 1\n22\t  open_questions: -1\n23\t  external_dependency: -1\n24\t  human_process_gates: 0\n25\t  repo_access: 1\n26\t  architecture_claims: 1\n27\timplementation_type: null\n28\tinvestigation_signals: null\n29\tai_implementability: Medium\n30\tai_implementability_score: 2\n31\tjira_key: null\n32\tbranch: null\n33\t---\n34\t# Productize supported vLLM ROCm serving runtime\n35\t\n36\t## Description\n37\t\n38\tProductize a supported vLLM ROCm serving runtime for the models cleared by\n39\tthe AMD Instinct validation campaign: build and release the ROCm runtime\n40\timage variant, package it as a platform serving runtime, and validate KServe\n41\tcompatibility on AMD GPU nodes. The runtime's supported scope is definitionally\n42\tthe set of models the validation campaign clears; if fewer models clear than\n43\tthe full supported set, this epic productizes the cleared subset.\n44\t\n45\t## Scope\n46\t\n47\t- Build and release a vLLM ROCm runtime image variant from the midstream vLLM\n48\t  repo, pinned to a recorded ROCm base image version from upstream releases.\n49\t- Configure the Konflux build pipeline for the ROCm image variant in the\n50\t  already-onboarded Serving Runtimes build machinery (no separate onboarding\n51\t  needed — the component is Konflux-onboarded).\n52\t- Define and ship the ServingRuntime (or ClusterServingRuntime) for the ROCm\n53\t  vLLM runtime, requesting amd.com/gpu resources and targeting AMD Instinct\n54\t  nodes.\n55\t- Validate KServe compatibility (KServe itself requires no code changes —\n56\t  accelerator support is runtime-level): InferenceServices using the ROCm\n57\t  serving runtime deploy and reach Ready on AMD GPU nodes.\n58\t- Record the supported (cleared) model set in the runtime's support\n59\t  metadata.\n60\t- Ensure coexistence with existing CUDA-based serving runtimes — the ROCm\n61\t  runtime is additive; existing runtimes are unaffected.\n62\t\n63\t## Acceptance Criteria\n64\t\n65\t- A vLLM ROCm runtime image build exists in the midstream repo, pinned to a\n66\t  recorded ROCm base image version.\n67\t- The Konflux build pipeline for the ROCm image variant is green.\n68\t- A ServingRuntime CR deploys the ROCm vLLM runtime with amd.com/gpu\n69\t  resource requests for the cleared model set.\n70\t- KServe InferenceServices using the ROCm serving runtime reach Ready on AMD\n71\t  GPU nodes.\n72\t- Existing CUDA-based serving runtimes deploy and serve unchanged (no\n73\t  regression; the new runtime is additive).\n74\t- The supported (cleared) model set is recorded in the runtime's support\n75\t  metadata.\n76\t\n77\t## HLR Traceability\n78\t\n79\t- HLR-2 (P0): a supported vLLM ROCm serving runtime is productized for the\n80\t  models the validation campaign clears.\n81\t- Supports HLR-4 inputs: the recorded supported model set feeds the\n82\t  documentation.\n83\t\n84\t## Risks and Notes\n85\t\n86\t- **Upstream ROCm image cadence (externally controlled):** whether AMD's\n87\t  runtime image releases align with our release trains is outside our\n88\t  control; a pinning/mirroring strategy for the ROCm base image may be\n89\t  needed to keep the productized runtime aligned with release trains.\n90\t- Scope is gated by the validation campaign's go/no-go outcome: if no models\n91\t  clear, productization is cancelled and the campaign report feeds a\n92\t  follow-up strategy decision.\n93\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-927d4619cc55007a","agent_id":"a7446498ab1d5d72c","session_id":"e88daf40-577f-4130-9c11-b6a9bfbaa4d6","uuid":"c10b07d1-af2b-4f7c-8eae-447887baf4c4","timestamp":"2026-10-26T18:23:21.612Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-922bd317edbf0add","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-9020"}
