{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-bfe8af90795bebb3","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9020-E003\n3\ttitle: PyTorch ROCm training support in the Training Operator\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9020\n5\tcomponent: Training Operator\n6\tteam: Distributed Workloads\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P1\n9\tai_signals:\n10\t  change_specificity: 0\n11\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n12\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n13\t  existing_foundation: 1\n14\t  open_questions: 0\n15\t  external_dependency: 0\n16\t  human_process_gates: 0\n17\t  repo_access: 1\n18\t  architecture_claims: 1\n19\timplementation_type: null\n20\tdependencies: []\n21\tinvestigation_signals: null\n22\tai_implementability: High\n23\tai_implementability_score: 4\n24\tjira_key: null\n25\tbranch: null\n26\tgated_by: null\n27\tgate_failure_impact: null\n28\t---\n29\t# PyTorch ROCm training support in the Training Operator\n30\t\n31\t## Description\n32\t\n33\tEnable PyTorch training on ROCm through the Training Operator: single-GPU and\n34\tmulti-GPU (distributed) PyTorchJobs scheduling and running on AMD Instinct\n35\tnodes using PyTorch ROCm worker images, with admission through Kueue covered\n36\tby the platform's queueing stack.\n37\t\n38\t## Scope\n39\t\n40\t- Enable PyTorchJob worker pods to schedule and run on AMD GPU nodes with\n41\t  amd.com/gpu resource requests (node placement on AMD Instinct nodes).\n42\t- Support single-GPU and multi-GPU (distributed) PyTorchJob topologies on\n43\t  ROCm.\n44\t- Use and document verified/pinned PyTorch ROCm worker image references for\n45\t  supported training jobs.\n46\t- Validate training execution on AMD Instinct hardware: jobs run to\n47\t  completion and distributed initialization works across workers for\n48\t  multi-GPU topologies.\n49\t\n50\t## Acceptance Criteria\n51\t\n52\t- A single-GPU PyTorchJob requesting amd.com/gpu resources runs to completion\n53\t  on AMD Instinct nodes.\n54\t- A multi-GPU PyTorchJob requesting amd.com/gpu resources runs to completion\n55\t  on AMD Instinct nodes with distributed initialization across workers.\n56\t- Verified/pinned PyTorch ROCm worker image references are documented for\n57\t  supported training jobs.\n58\t- Existing NVIDIA GPU PyTorchJob execution is unaffected (no regression; AMD\n59\t  support is additive).\n60\t\n61\t## HLR Traceability\n62\t\n63\t- HLR-3 (P1): PyTorch training on ROCm is supported for single- and\n64\t  multi-GPU jobs admitted through Kueue, with amd.com/gpu quota handling\n65\t  (quota/admission side covered by the Distributed Workloads epic).\n66\t\n67\t## Risks and Notes\n68\t\n69\t- **Physical hardware dependency:** validation requires physical AMD Instinct\n70\t  nodes, the same hardware whose access path (procurement vs. partner lab) is\n71\t  unresolved for the serving validation campaign. This is a shared\n72\t  resource-coordination risk, not a structural dependency on the serving\n73\t  campaign's outcome — training enablement proceeds independently.\n74\t- PyTorch ROCm worker images are published upstream; no upstream\n75\t  contribution is required, but available image versions follow the upstream\n76\t  release cadence.\n77\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-927d4619cc55007a","agent_id":"a7446498ab1d5d72c","session_id":"e88daf40-577f-4130-9c11-b6a9bfbaa4d6","uuid":"f45f45e7-4a21-4633-b90f-7d56ce9fd582","timestamp":"2026-10-26T18:23:22.338Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-bfe8af90795bebb3","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-9020"}
