{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-ac951b775ea90ad9","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9020-E004\n3\ttitle: Kueue amd.com/gpu quota handling for ROCm training workloads\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9020\n5\tcomponent: Distributed Workloads\n6\tteam: Distributed Workloads\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P1\n9\tai_signals:\n10\t  change_specificity: 1\n11\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n12\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n13\t  existing_foundation: 1\n14\t  open_questions: 0\n15\t  external_dependency: 0\n16\t  human_process_gates: 0\n17\t  repo_access: 1\n18\t  architecture_claims: 1\n19\timplementation_type: null\n20\tdependencies: []\n21\tinvestigation_signals: null\n22\tai_implementability: High\n23\tai_implementability_score: 5\n24\tjira_key: null\n25\tbranch: null\n26\tgated_by: null\n27\tgate_failure_impact: null\n28\t---\n29\t# Kueue amd.com/gpu quota handling for ROCm training workloads\n30\t\n31\t## Description\n32\t\n33\tEnable and validate quota handling for amd.com/gpu resources in the\n34\tDistributed Workloads stack so that PyTorch training jobs on ROCm are admitted\n35\tthrough Kueue with correct quota accounting and all-or-nothing (gang)\n36\tsemantics for multi-GPU jobs.\n37\t\n38\t## Scope\n39\t\n40\t- Quota configuration for amd.com/gpu resources in the Kueue quota model\n41\t  (ClusterQueue/LocalQueue) covering AMD GPU node flavors.\n42\t- Admission of single- and multi-GPU PyTorchJobs requesting amd.com/gpu\n43\t  through Kueue, with all-or-nothing admission for multi-GPU job topologies.\n44\t- Validate quota accounting: admitted workloads' amd.com/gpu usage counts\n45\t  against configured quota, and workloads queue when quota is exhausted.\n46\t- Verify no regression to existing NVIDIA GPU quota handling and admission.\n47\t\n48\t## Acceptance Criteria\n49\t\n50\t- ClusterQueue/LocalQueue quota configuration supports amd.com/gpu resources\n51\t  for AMD GPU node flavors.\n52\t- A single-GPU PyTorchJob requesting amd.com/gpu is admitted through Kueue\n53\t  against the configured quota.\n54\t- A multi-GPU PyTorchJob requesting amd.com/gpu is admitted with\n55\t  all-or-nothing semantics under the amd.com/gpu quota.\n56\t- Quota accounting for amd.com/gpu is correct: usage of admitted workloads is\n57\t  reflected in quota consumption, and workloads queue when quota is\n58\t  exhausted.\n59\t- Existing NVIDIA GPU quota handling and admission behave unchanged.\n60\t\n61\t## HLR Traceability\n62\t\n63\t- HLR-3 (P1): PyTorch training on ROCm is supported for single- and\n64\t  multi-GPU jobs admitted through Kueue, with amd.com/gpu quota handling\n65\t  (job execution side covered by the Training Operator epic).\n66\t\n67\t## Risks and Notes\n68\t\n69\t- **Physical hardware dependency:** end-to-end admission validation requires\n70\t  AMD GPU nodes and a runnable ROCm training workload; this shares the\n71\t  unresolved AMD hardware access path with the serving validation campaign\n72\t  (resource-coordination risk, not a structural dependency).\n73\t- Coordinating a shared end-to-end validation run (a multi-GPU ROCm\n74\t  PyTorchJob admitted under amd.com/gpu quota) with the Training Operator\n75\t  work is a planning concern; each side's acceptance criteria can be verified\n76\t  independently.\n77\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-927d4619cc55007a","agent_id":"a7446498ab1d5d72c","session_id":"e88daf40-577f-4130-9c11-b6a9bfbaa4d6","uuid":"7165ea2c-11d1-4d90-8de9-97cc2d00b82f","timestamp":"2026-10-26T18:23:22.964Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-ac951b775ea90ad9","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-9020"}
